How sure: fairly sure about the pattern (about 85%). The exact mechanism inside 5.2 is not yet confirmed.

What to do next: revert 5.2's adaptive-streaming settings in Kestria to the 5.1 behaviour and pause the wider 5.2 rollout until fixed. Do not approve the Tessaline breach notice, the fee withholding or the move back to Corvane, since they target the wrong cause. Keep the Kestria rebuffering alert on, and add app version and device breakdowns to the dashboard, although that needs a pipeline rebuild that is about six weeks away. Treat the cancellation link as unproven before offering refunds.","methodChoice":"Collected one item (X10), the playback breakdown by app, version and ISP, which discriminated between the CDN and app-release explanations."}
